      "content": "Wait, really? I actually thought the opposite. To me, Sterling's abstract (Abstract 1) felt much more sophisticated with terms like 'cortical thinning' and 'cognitive plasticity'. Adeyemi's (Abstract 2) seemed a bit more... I don't know, plain? \n\nWhy do you think Abstract 2 is the more \"authoritative\" one? I'm trying to understand if you're picking up on something in the prose that I'm missing, or if it's just a matter of preference.",
