      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, thanks for clarifying. I guess I was just surprised because you initially flagged the more technical one as potentially \"popular science\" and the simpler one as \"standard journal style.\" \n\nSince you're helping me with these reviews, do you think the author's background or name plays any role in how these linguistic styles are perceived? Like, when you're analyzing \"voice,\" do you find that certain academic styles are more closely associated with certain regions or demographics? I'm just wondering if there's a systematic way these \"authoritative\" tones are tied to specific cultural backgrounds in the literature you've been trained on.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
